abstract: >-
  VarioCorreKrigE is a Python-based geostatistical toolkit
  developed for simple to advanced spatial analysis, with
  particular emphasis on earthquake engineering and
  natural‑hazard applications rather than full geophysical
  forward modelling. The framework integrates experimental
  variogram and correlogram estimation, parametric model
  fitting, auto‑ and cross‑dependence analysis, grouped and
  multivariate workflows, and kriging-based spatial
  interpolation within a consistent and extensible
  environment. While engineered primarily for analysing
  spatially distributed variables such as ground‑motion
  intensities, residuals, site-condition proxies, and other
  engineering-relevant datasets, the package also
  accommodates both distance‑based and angular dependence
  structures.


  Importantly, VarioCorreKrigE also supports traditional
  geophysical spatial‑estimation techniques including
  cokriging, collocated cokriging, and related multivariate
  interpolation methods which can be used as exploratory
  tools or as part of more formal dependence‑modelling
  workflows. In addition, the framework incorporates
  advanced statistical capabilities such as variogram and
  correlogram bootstrapping for pseudo‑posterior parameter
  estimation, as well as a full implementation of empirical
  Bayesian kriging (EBK) for propagating parameter
  uncertainty into spatial predictions. By combining robust
  estimation procedures, flexible covariance and correlation
  modelling, and practical visualisation tools,
  VarioCorreKrigE provides a reproducible platform for
  characterising spatial variability, quantifying
  dependence, and supporting engineering decision‑making in
  seismic and broader natural‑hazard contexts.
